          "content": "Short answer\n- Choose an LED task lamp (adjustable arm/head, dimmable) that meets these efficiency/quality criteria below. From your product catalog I found the \"Meadowlight Lamp\" (a standard office desk lamp). The catalog entry does not include technical specs, so Meadowlight may be a candidate but its energy-efficiency claims need verification (see details).\n\nWhy an LED task lamp\n- LEDs provide the best combination of lumen output per watt, long life, and low maintenance vs incandescent/halogen/fluorescent.\n- Look for dimming and targeted task lighting (swing arm, adjustable head) so you can use less total light when full output isn’t needed.\n- Certifications (ENERGY STAR, DLC) and measured efficacy (lm/W) are the most reliable indicators of energy performance.\n\nSelection checklist (what to require and why)\n- Light source: LED (best energy per lumen).\n- Efficacy: ≥ 80–100 lm/W is good for task lighting — higher is more efficient. Verify actual lm/W from the spec sheet.\n- Output (lumens): 400–1,200 lm depending on how bright you need the desk area to be.\n- Color temperature: 3000–4000 K for office comfort (neutral/warm white). Pick based on preference.\n- CRI: ≥ 80 (≥ 90 if color accuracy is important).\n- Dimming: Yes — supports continuous dimming (0–100%) without color shift.\n- Controls: physical dimmer + optional occupancy sensor or daylight sensor for extra savings.\n- Mounting: clamp or compact base and adjustable arm for precise task lighting.\n- Warranty & rated life: lifetime rating (e.g., 30,000–50,000 hours) and a multi-year warranty.\n- Certification: ENERGY STAR or DLC listed for validated energy performance.\n- Flicker: low flicker / meets IEEE/IEC recommendations (important for comfort).\n\nCatalog product found in memory\n- Meadowlight Lamp — memory extract: “The Meadowlight Lamp is a standard desk lamp sold for offices.”\n  - Provenance: entry in your catalog memory (entity id 3dd1ec13-ccb0-4986-9f91-9f8bd0bc8389